    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40766" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕd-uncus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>curved</i> or <i>bent backwards</i>
			(very rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syn.: recurvus, repandus): jamque aliis adunca,
					aliis redunca (cornua dedit),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 45, § 125</span></i>
			.— <b>Poet.</b>, in gen., <i>curved</i>, <i>bent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pennis rostroque redunco,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 562</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ora redunca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 11, 342</span></i>
			.</div>
